    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant upside at the top of the order, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Trea Turner** (77.93). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our clear standout; he draws a favorable matchup against Dobnak (5.16 xERA) and benefits from a 14% boost due to platoon advantage and a 5% wind-aid, making him a primary source for our critical stolen base production. Similarly, **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.21) find themselves in prime scoring positions against Bieber. Despite Bieber\u2019s pedigree, his 5.23 xERA suggests vulnerability, and the combination of the #1 and #2 spots in the order provides a high-leverage opportunity for **Kyle Schwarber** and **Trea Turner** to anchor our R and RBI totals. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in elite start at 68.54, providing a high floor regardless of his pending official lineup confirmation.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved the marginal range of our utility options, specifically why **Josh Smith** (33.53) was benched in favor of **Gary Sanchez** (49.62). While **Gary Sanchez** carries a lower raw base, his platoon advantage against the lefty Prielipp pushed him over the Zurich Zebras' floor of 40.0. **Josh Smith** ultimately fell short due to his unfavorable platoon split against Luzardo and his low-leverage #8 spot in the order, which further compressed his scoring potential. We are also monitoring **Junior Caminero** (61.00), who holds the highest score among our infielders; despite the pitcher's park, his strong xwOBA (0.378) makes him a reliable start over the more volatile **Dillon Dingler** (40.41), whose dynamic platoon penalty against Webb significantly hampered his daily efficiency.\n\nWe are operating with a relatively clean slate, though owners should note the inherent risk in **Dillon Dingler**'s matchup against Webb, as the SP Skill penalty (-2%) and platoon disadvantage make him a high-variance play. We have excluded **Christian Yelich**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Lars Nootbaar** from today's active roster entirely due to their status as bench, IL, or rest, as we prioritize maximizing our daily game caps. With **Kazuma Okamoto** (48.21) and **Colt Keith** (53.46) providing solid middle-infield production, the Zebras are well-positioned to maintain category leads provided our speed specialists, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Trea Turner**, capitalize on the favorable SP xERA metrics present across today\u2019s matchups.",
